---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Feedback from "../../components/Feedback.astro";
import m from "../../data/pipe_blockages/metrics.json";
import { STREAMLIT_URL } from "../../config";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const fig = (name: string) => `${base}data/pipe_blockages/figures/${name}.png`;
const pctOf = (x: number) => `${Math.round(x * 100)}%`;
const eff = m.tree_effect;
const toolUrl = STREAMLIT_URL ? `${STREAMLIT_URL}/Pipe_Blockages` : "";
const drivers = m.drivers.filter((d) => !d.term.endsWith("_missing") && !["relined", "depth (per m)"].includes(d.term));
const nice: Record<string, string> = {
  "diameter (per 100 mm)": "Each extra 100 mm of diameter",
  "age (per 10 years)": "Each extra 10 years of age",
  "slope (per 1%)": "Each extra 1% of slope",
  trees_5m: "Each tree within 5 m",
  aggressive_trees_10m: "Each root-aggressive tree within 10 m",
};
const label = (t: string) => nice[t] ?? t.replace("material: ", "") + " pipe (vs plastic)";
const change = (irr: number) => (irr >= 1 ? `+${Math.round((irr - 1) * 100)}%` : `−${Math.round((1 - irr) * 100)}%`);
const clear = (d: { ci: number[] }) => !(d.ci[0] < 1 && d.ci[1] > 1);
---
<Base
  title="Which sewer pipes block, and do trees cause it? · Christchurch Projects"
  description={m.headline}
  dataPulledAt={m.data_pulled_at}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Which sewer pipes block, and do trees cause it?</h1>
    <p class="headline">{m.headline}</p>

    <div class="cta">
      {toolUrl
        ? <a id="open-tool" class="btn btn-primary" href={toolUrl}>Open the interactive tool: map, your street, top 20 to inspect →</a>
        : <p class="muted">Interactive tool coming soon.</p>}
    </div>

    <section class="stats" aria-label="Key numbers">
      <div class="card stat"><span class="n">{m.n_pipes.toLocaleString("en-NZ")}</span><span>sewer pipes analysed ({Math.round(m.km).toLocaleString("en-NZ")} km)</span></div>
      <div class="card stat"><span class="n">{m.total_blockages.toLocaleString("en-NZ")}</span><span>recorded blockages (all time)</span></div>
      <div class="card stat"><span class="n">{pctOf(m.cv.top_decile_capture)}</span><span>of blockages in the riskiest 10% of pipe, vs {pctOf(m.cv.baseline_top_decile_capture)} by material alone</span></div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="trees-h">
      <h2 id="trees-h">Do trees cause blockages?</h2>
      <p class="tree-answer"><strong>{eff.sentence.replace("There is no clear evidence", "There is no clear evidence")}</strong></p>
      <p>That doesn't mean roots never block sewers. The council's open data records street and park trees, not
        private garden trees, which are the usual suspects for roots in older household connections. Where street trees
        are planted (newer, wider streets with newer pipes) also hides any effect.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="drivers-h">
      <h2 id="drivers-h">What does make a pipe block</h2>
      <p class="muted">Change in recorded blockages, with everything else held equal (95% confidence interval).</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Factor</th><th scope="col">Effect</th><th scope="col">Range</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {drivers.map((d) => (
            <tr class={clear(d) ? "" : "muted"}>
              <td>{label(d.term)}</td>
              <td><strong>{change(d.irr)}</strong></td>
              <td>{change(d.ci[0])} to {change(d.ci[1])}{clear(d) ? "" : " (not clear)"}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="charts-h">
      <h2 id="charts-h">The evidence</h2>
      <div class="figs">
        <figure class="card"><img src={fig("rate_by_material")} alt="Bar chart: recorded blockages per km by pipe material. Earthenware, asbestos cement and concrete are highest; plastic lowest." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Blockages per km by material, before allowing for age and size.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="card"><img src={fig("rate_by_trees")} alt="Bar chart: blockages per km by number of recorded trees within 5 m. Pipes with no recorded trees have the highest rate." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Pipes with <em>no</em> recorded trees nearby block most. That's a location effect, not trees protecting pipes.</figcaption></figure>
        <figure class="card"><img src={fig("rate_by_age_material")} alt="Line chart: blockage rate rises with pipe age for older materials." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Older pipes block more. Very old "plastic" pipes are renewed pipes that kept their original install date.</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="how-h">
      <h2 id="how-h">About this analysis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>In-service, council-owned gravity sewer pipes; recorded blockages are all-time and undated, so there are no trends.</li>
        <li>Findings are associations, not proof of cause. Relined pipes are relined <em>because</em> they blocked, so relining is never used to rank risk.</li>
        <li>Validated on areas the model never saw (1 km grid cells held out).</li>
        <li>Full write-up: <a href="https://github.com/hyunjinlee0131-wq/christchurch-projects/blob/main/projects/pipe_blockages/SUMMARY.md">executive summary</a>{" "}and{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/hyunjinlee0131-wq/christchurch-projects/blob/main/projects/pipe_blockages/eda.ipynb">analysis notebook</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <Feedback project="pipe_blockages" itemId="summary" question="Was this useful?" />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .headline { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; max-width: 48rem; }
  .cta { margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .cta .btn { display: inline-block; text-decoration: none; }
  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .stat { display: grid; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .stat .n { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .tree-answer { font-size: 1.1rem; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); border-radius: var(--radius); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  th { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .figs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  figure { margin: 0; }
  figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: 6px; background: #fff; }
  figcaption { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
</style>
